# TODO - Typed compiler IR

## Objective

Define a small deterministic IR representing control flow, arithmetic, memory,
calls, byte I/O, target-profile requirements, and proof obligations without
inheriting unnecessary LLVM complexity.

## Acceptance

- The IR has a documented closed grammar/type system for control flow,
  arithmetic, memory, calls, byte I/O, profile requirements, and proof
  obligations plus deterministic serialization/debug printing.
- The stage has deterministic input/output form, rejects malformed or
  unsupported input explicitly, and preserves source/profile provenance needed
  downstream.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `compiler/`, `src/`, `tests/compiler/`.
- Required evidence: golden/round-trip or normalized stage fixtures,
  deterministic hashes where promised, and end-to-end lowering regression cases.
- Implemented model evidence: governed `src/compiler/typed-ir/` now owns the
  safe Rust `malbolge-typed-ir-v1` model for explicit dense IDs, portable types,
  typed SSA/basic blocks, automatic storage, direct/indirect calls, byte I/O,
  terminators, source spans, and verifier-visible proof obligations.
- Implemented admission evidence: the application boundary validates closed
  version/ABI/profile identity, type references, unique/dense symbols and SSA,
  complete reachability, entry-block phi prohibition, exact phi predecessors,
  SSA dominance including phi edges, owner-contained provenance spans,
  operand/result types, calls, memory
  alignment/pointee relationships,
  control-flow types, exact constants, explicit bool/integer promotions,
  adjusted function signatures, default-promoted variadic arguments,
  automatic-allocation shape, direct/indirect call targets,
  object-only SSA/globals, object-pointer memory proofs, generic `void *`
  membership in the object-pointer namespace, exact 32-bit
  object-pointer/integer
  conversions, and proof references including structural
  no-signed-overflow result association.
- Implemented identity evidence: canonicalization validates first, emits `MCTI`
  version-one bytes with explicit little-endian fields, checked `u32` lengths,
  and repository-owned enum tags, then derives deterministic lowercase-hex
  debug identity. A tracked golden locks the accepted diamond-CFG artifact.
- Implemented regression evidence: `tests/compiler_ir.rs` currently covers 68
  accepted/rejected cases including duplicate SSA, use-before-definition,
  unreachable CFG, phi predecessor/edge dominance, direct/indirect calls,
  automatic allocation, object-type, proof/type/provenance, branch/constant,
  invalid load alignment, normalized frontend lowering, explicit bool casts,
  function-pointer memory proofs, finite aggregate layout, and global
  initializer extent failures, source-span containment violations, and the
  ABI-defined signed plain-`char` category, strict object/function pointer
  separation, C integer/default-argument promotions, adjusted array signatures,
  proof-result association, and exact pointer/integer encoding width.
- Implemented layout evidence: application admission computes canonical ABI
  scalar/array/struct/union extent with checked 32-bit arithmetic, rejects
  by-value recursive aggregates, and requires explicit global initializer bytes
  to match the exact declared object extent.
- Implemented frontend-lowering evidence: a typed inbound semantic projection
  carries exact `malbolge-c-frontend-v1` producer identity, declaration facts,
  source hash, and normalized spans. The initial lowerer accepts only a defined
  external non-inline `fn()->i32` integer-constant return, preserves provenance,
  runs complete IR admission, and has a tracked canonical typed-IR golden.
- Real-frontend fixture evidence: pinned Clang 22.1.8 normalizes tracked
  `ir_return_constant.c` into an exact checked-in frontend JSON golden; the Rust
  lowering projection uses that golden's exact source digest/spans/semantics.
- Implemented quality evidence: the typed-IR implementation passes the full
  workspace nightly Clippy policy with warnings denied and uses no broad lint
  suppression to admit the new compiler surface.
- Boundary evidence: LLVM IR remains design prior art only; Clang AST identity,
  LLVM poison/undef/metadata, native data layout, and Malbolge target encoding
  are excluded from portable typed-IR authority.
- Completion boundary evidence: the typed-IR objective permits explicit
  unsupported-input failures. Broader normalized C coverage (linkable external
  symbols, aggregates, VLAs, addressable objects, and other accepted constructs)
  is transferred to `tools-tidy-lowerability-contract`, which cannot complete
  until every linter-clean accepted translation unit lowers through this stage.
  Ternary and target lowering remain owned by their dependent compiler stages.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `clang-c-frontend-integration`,
  `deterministic-c-to-malbolge-abi`.
- Completion evidence: closed grammar/type system, validation-gated canonical
  identity, real normalized-frontend-to-IR golden, explicit unsupported-input
  failures, source/profile provenance, and exhaustive repository validation are
  sufficient to retire this objective without losing deferred compiler coverage.
